// Title: Suspicious FromBase64String Usage On Gzip Archive - Process Creation
// Sigma ID: d75d6b6b-adb9-48f7-824b-ac2e786efe1f
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-12-23 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1132.001
// Description: Detects attempts of decoding a base64 Gzip archive via PowerShell. This technique is often used
//   as a method to load malicious content into memory afterward.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administrative script
// References:
//   - https://speakerdeck.com/heirhabarov/hunting-for-powershell-abuse?slide=43
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ad147b5514596e70f2782769d9833046b7c8e12b/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_powershell_frombase64string_archive.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "FromBase64String" and ProcessCommandLine contains "MemoryStream" and ProcessCommandLine contains "H4sI"
